2026-08-01: Profiled immutable scoring, task split geometry, table join coverage, temporal range, installed LightGBM API, and model-fit throughput. Added the time-allocation plan and root evaluation profile; the protected kapso_evaluation directory was not modified.
2026-08-01: Corrected qualifying coverage after detecting a profiling column-name collision: train coverage is 14.12%, validation 100%, and test 99.65%, with irregular historical availability through 2002.
2026-08-01: Replaced the trivial baseline with a 407-feature, all-table Formula 1 pipeline containing exact-current and season-aware strict-lag standings, qualifying, constructor results, race/circuit/entity attributes, group-relative and teammate features, and strict-prior target form.
2026-08-01: Added three-seed LightGBM L2, ordinal cumulative classifiers at 14 thresholds, race-grouped LambdaMART, OOF isotonic calibration, PAVA CDF rectification, Gaussian rank PMFs, and 50-iteration log-domain Sinkhorn decoding with unit marginal checks.
2026-08-01: Implemented three strict forward folds with fold-boundary label horizons, a pooled +0.005/worst-fold gate, reusable namespaced OOF caches registered under the shared cache, original-row restoration, and separate train-only validation versus train-plus-validation test chains.
2026-08-01: No external datasets or pretrained models were used. The protected kapso_evaluation directory and sanitized inputs were not modified.
2026-08-01 difficulties: Initial profiling reported 100% train qualifying coverage because the merge inspected the unsuffixed target column; inspecting qual_position after an explicit rename corrected it to 14.12%. Initial compile failed with SyntaxError at f1_features.py line 57 from an unclosed rank call; closing the call fixed it. The first feature build failed with pandas.errors.MergeError because historical shared-drive rows make the left (raceId, driverId) key non-unique; changing current qualifying/standings joins from one-to-one to many-to-one fixed it. Missing-indicator insertion emitted many pandas PerformanceWarning lines and fragmented output; constructing indicators as one frame and concatenating once fixed it. The first OOF history implementation was row-causal but allowed earlier held-out-fold labels; rebuilding form features from labels strictly before each fold boundary removed the horizon mismatch. Fixed-iteration Sinkhorn left residual row-mass errors up to 0.12 in debug; conditional means are now normalized by residual row mass, while the final 50-iteration selected configuration verified errors below 0.01. Race-atomic Elo v6 and short-window v7 were both rejected because full internal OOF R2 was below v5 despite slightly higher official-validation scores; the final code deliberately reverted to v5.
